  "body": "PR #1698 delivered the magazine barrel vault and genuine 25-member native build, but its completed SDK had no target 1812 body/Design/Sources browser review and no ROADMAP delivery note. This required completion of the visible magazine parcel records that delivery and supplies those missing checks. T-3041/T-2387 remain partial/open; the Currey comparison remains DIFFERS.\n\nOnly STATUS and ROADMAP append here. Their complete raw prefixes remain exact. No renderer, source grade, data, camera, geometry or native asset changes.\n\nValidation:\n- Actual published `d5fdc7d4c6` magazine review passed at 1280\u00d7800 (500.71s) and 390\u00d7780 (207.64s): clear native exterior, real GPU roof/body picks, real delegated parade ground, safe native ground arrival, and actual Inspect Design/Sources. Zero page/console/network/server errors; all processes properly closed. Arrival is stockade-obstructed and does not prove doorway traversal.\n- Native-centered Sources supplements passed both sizes (186.37s/113.30s). Whistler 1808/War Department/Quaife and Currey 1912 credits are readable, with inferred vault vs reconstructed rise/profile/covering and no new metric/date/colour claim. Initial sticky-header-clipped screenshots remain preserved.\n- [Full guarded runtime evidence](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-evidence/blob/38e7792be383556ed9506f3047e6fa2c041b7ea0/evidence/first-fort-2026-11-04/pr1699-current1812-magazine-body-design-sources/runtime-d5-v2/FINAL-CLOSURE.json), [source-credit supplement](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-evidence/blob/38e7792be383556ed9506f3047e6fa2c041b7ea0/evidence/first-fort-2026-11-04/pr1699-current1812-magazine-body-design-sources/sources-centered-d5/FINAL-CLOSURE.json), [direct pixel review](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-evidence/blob/38e7792be383556ed9506f3047e6fa2c041b7ea0/evidence/first-fort-2026-11-04/pr1699-current1812-magazine-body-design-sources/DIRECT-PIXEL-REVIEW.json).\n- Final source `880036af3d6355799968fea9a77b92d85f95deec` differs from executed D5 only by the two append-only docs. All 19,207 other tracked entries are exact; this carries the browser result through runtime-consumer equivalence, rather than claiming a new execution on final hash.\n- Docs/changelog policy/shape/raw-prefix/ID checks pass. D5's hosted eight-part gate and aggregate passed. Final exact-head hosted eight-part gate and aggregate: RUNNING, run 41802166800. Auto-merge remains off pending final qualification.\n\nThe first desktop fixture used the raw-sidecar expectation rather than actual consumed readerCopy; its RED result and unrun phone are preserved publicly. Corrected separate guarded legs passed. Historical generic 1835 107/0 results predate the native PR's final renderer integration and are not relabelled as current executions; no generic/native bake was repeated. Earlier local source-part-4/NumPy RED remains retained separately from the final hosted command's pass. No production promotion or whole-fort picture acceptance is claimed.\n\nIndependent root [direct pixel review](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-evidence/blob/5c1848b84ce9c09050f48b78fdb2c921afa72fb8/evidence/first-fort-2026-11-04/pr1699-final-docs-880-root-pixels-checkpoint/ROOT-PIXEL-REVIEW.json) accepted the bounded exterior/Design/credit frames. [Final docs-only runtime carry and qualification](https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-evidence/blob/5c1848b84ce9c09050f48b78fdb2c921afa72fb8/evidence/first-fort-2026-11-04/pr1699-final-docs-880-root-pixels-checkpoint/FINAL-DOCS-RUNTIME-CARRY.json) is saved publicly with the immutable source handoff.\n",
